window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["1e"]={"https://theconversation.com/avoiding-the-f-word-australia-and-turkey-dance-around-fossil-fuels-at-cop31-summit-296418":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"04d974b1884e74538916552cf8cb725f2c5da48f637eab87f07606431e52f693","read":"https://theconversation.com/avoiding-the-f-word-australia-and-turkey-dance-around-fossil-fuels-at-cop31-summit-296418","bytes":188202,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Avoiding the ‘F word’: Australia and Turkey dance around fossil fuels at COP31 summit","by":[{"n":"Matt McDonald","r":"Professor of International Relations, The University of Queensland"}],"pub":"2026-11-13T04:21:18Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["One phrase has been glaringly absent from this year’s ",["COP31 climate summit","https://theconversation.com/plenty-of-reasons-for-hope-what-30-years-of-climate-talks-have-achieved-296398"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fossil fuels are not mentioned in the COP31 ",["priority areas","https://www.genevaenvironmentnetwork.org/resources/updates/climate-action-from-geneva-to-antalya-un-climate-change-conference-cop31/"],". Key speeches from the leaders of Australia and Turkey (Türkiye), co-hosts of the conference, have largely ",["failed to address","https://unfccc.int/news/transcript-of-press-conference-opening-remarks-today-of-cop31-president-president-of-negotiations-un"]," the emissions-shaped elephant in the room."]},{"k":"p","s":["That’s despite mounting pressure from ",["environmental groups","https://www.greenpeace.org/international/story/86619/cop31-antalya/"],", ",["Pacific nations","https://theconversation.com/australias-climate-minister-is-about-to-walk-a-diplomatic-tightrope-at-cop31-294565"]," and COP30 host nation ",["Brazil","https://ipam.org.br/cop31-ipam-highlights-lulas-call-for-action-against-the-climate-crisis/"]," to abandon coal, oil and gas and slash global emissions."]},{"k":"p","s":["So why does this matter? And what does it mean for climate action worldwide?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["‘Plenty of reasons for hope’: what 30 years of climate talks have achieved","https://theconversation.com/plenty-of-reasons-for-hope-what-30-years-of-climate-talks-have-achieved-296398"]]},{"k":"h","s":["A strange absence"]},{"k":"p","s":["In their opening speeches, neither Turkish President ",["Recep Tayyip Erdoğan","https://www.akparti.org.tr/en/main-slider-news/president-recep-tayyip-erdogan-delivered-a-speech-at-the-cop31-leaders-summit-opening-event-in-antalya-11-11-2026-15-00-00/"]," nor Australian Prime Minister ",["Anthony Albanese","https://www.pm.gov.au/media/cop31-leaders-summit-opening-ceremony"]," mentioned fossil fuels."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the official commencement of COP31, the Australian president of negotiations and environment minister, ",["Chris Bowen","https://unfccc.int/news/transcript-of-press-conference-opening-remarks-today-of-cop31-president-president-of-negotiations-un"],", twice uttered the words fossil fuels. Neither reference was tied to specific goals for a global fossil fuel phase out or weaning Australia, one of the world’s ",["largest exporters","https://theconversation.com/dug-up-in-australia-burned-around-the-world-exporting-fossil-fuels-undermines-climate-targets-236248"]," of coal and gas, off them. In his opening remarks, Turkey’s environment minister ",["Murat Kurum","https://unfccc.int/news/transcript-of-press-conference-opening-remarks-today-of-cop31-president-president-of-negotiations-un"]," didn’t mention them at all."]},{"k":"p","s":["This reluctance to spotlight fossil fuels is also reflected in the priority areas, or main aims, of COP31 that were agreed by the co-host nations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The headline goal is the “ ",["35-by-35","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-10/cop31-tingle-global-temperature-1-5c/107366402?utm_source=abc_news_app&utm_medium=content_shared&utm_campaign=abc_news_app&utm_content=link"],"” target to produce 35% of the world’s energy from electricity, increasingly using renewables, by 2035. Other priorities include halving the growth of ",["global waste","https://unfccc.int/news/un-secretary-general-s-remarks-to-the-leaders-roundtable-zero-waste-circularity-and-methane"]," and cutting energy consumption in the ",["building sector","https://unfccc.int/news/cop31-presidency-announces-new-targets-on-global-electrification-cutting-waste-resilient-cities"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, nowhere in sight is a plan or timeline to eliminate fossil fuels."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Global carbon emissions may have peaked in 2026 – but only time will tell","https://theconversation.com/global-carbon-emissions-may-have-peaked-in-2026-but-only-time-will-tell-296152"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Why the reluctance?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Negotiators may point to previous COPs, where the very mention of fossil fuels has sparked contention. At COP30 in Brazil, major oil producers Russia and Saudi Arabia ",["fought hard","https://theconversation.com/cop30-petrostates-block-climate-deal-once-again-but-some-countries-are-taking-their-own-decisive-steps-to-phase-out-fossil-fuels-270580"]," to ensure fossil fuels did not feature in the final agreed text. In comparison, the 2035 electrification goal may be more likely to ",["achieve consensus","https://www.theage.com.au/environment/climate-change/harry-kewell-was-his-neighbour-paul-keating-was-his-hero-the-making-of-climate-change-minister-chris-bowen-20261030-p616rm.html?collection=p619gp&gb=1"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But there’s a simpler explanation for this fossil fuel avoidance: any discussion of these fuels would undermine the credibility of the co-host nations as climate leaders, given their common reliance on coal, oil and gas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia is the world’s ",["third-largest exporter","https://www.climatecouncil.org.au/momentum-monitor-kpi/fossil-fuel-exports/"]," of fossil fuels, behind only Russia and the United States. These offshore emissions bring Australia’s total emissions ",["close to 5%","https://climateanalytics.org/publications/evaluating-the-significance-of-australias-global-fossil-fuel-carbon-footprint"]," of the global footprint. What’s more, Australia ",["continued approving","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-09/global-emissions-footprint-overshadows-australias-image/107329288?utm_source=abc_news_app&utm_medium=content_shared&utm_campaign=abc_news_app&utm_content=link"]," new fossil fuel mining projects, even after its role at COP31 was confirmed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Turkey is not a fossil fuel exporter but remains a ",["major consumer","https://www.theenergymix.com/cop31-host-turkiye-co-president-australia-falling-short-on-clean-energy-electrification-pledge/"]," of them, ",["particularly coal","https://www.worldometers.info/coal/coal-consumption-by-country/"],". On the eve of COP31 talks, Turkish President Erdogan ",["was criticised","https://www.arabnews.com/middle-east/erdogan-hails-new-oil-find-ahead-of-cop31-speech-3010886"]," for celebrating the discovery of two significant new oil fields."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Dug up in Australia, burned around the world – exporting fossil fuels undermines climate targets","https://theconversation.com/dug-up-in-australia-burned-around-the-world-exporting-fossil-fuels-undermines-climate-targets-236248"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Not totally off the table"]},{"k":"p","s":["Abandoning fossil fuels clearly ",["isn’t a priority","https://www.japantimes.co.jp/environment/2026/11/04/climate-change/cop31-brazil-fossil-fuel/"]," of this year’s hosting team. But this doesn’t necessarily extend to other nations attending COP31."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the lead-up to COP31, civil society and environmental groups, including ",["Greenpeace","https://www.greenpeace.org/international/story/86619/cop31-antalya/"]," and ",["Amnesty","https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/11/cop31-world-leaders-must-break-fossil-fuels-grip-on-climate-policy/"],", voiced their disappointment that fossil fuels were largely left out of the official agenda. While recognising the headline goals as worthy aims, some organisations criticised the agenda as being not ambitious enough, given the scale of the climate crisis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pacific countries have also pushed hard for an end to fossil fuels, notably through a ",["fossil fuel treaty","https://www.fossilfueltreaty.org/tassiriki-call"]," that would establish concrete plans and timelines. These small island nations have also declared Australia’s approval of new fossil fuel projects as “ ",["immoral and unacceptable","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/oct/01/australia-coalmine-decision-akin-to-drowning-its-pacific-neighbours-tuvalu-climate-minister-says?CMP=Share_iOSApp_Other"],"”. This criticism is particularly telling, given Australia made its co-hosting bid with the aim of spotlighting the climate vulnerability of its ",["Pacific neighbours","https://news.uq.edu.au/2026-11-what-you-need-know-about-cop31"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Brazil","https://www.smh.com.au/politics/federal/fossil-fuels-must-go-the-way-of-the-dinosaurs-un-boss-pushes-australia-to-go-further-20261112-p61dfw.html"]," has also emerged as a vocal critic of this year’s co-hosts. After leading the preceding COP30 conference, Brazil formally presented its ",["global roadmap","https://cop30.br/en/news-about-cop30/roadmap-taff"]," for transitioning away from fossil fuels to several high-profile UN leaders, ",["making a splash","https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/11/1168775"]," on the second day of COP31 negotiations. The roadmap is a practical guide offering targets, timetables and other considerations to help countries shift away from fossil fuels. After speaking to the challenge of climate change, newly re-elected President ",["Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva","https://ipam.org.br/cop31-ipam-highlights-lulas-call-for-action-against-the-climate-crisis/"]," urged his COP31 audience to turn the roadmap into concrete action."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Australia’s climate minister is about to walk a diplomatic tightrope at COP31","https://theconversation.com/australias-climate-minister-is-about-to-walk-a-diplomatic-tightrope-at-cop31-294565"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Why does this matter?"]},{"k":"p","s":["This debate over whether to call out the world’s reliance on fossil fuels is problematic, not least because it points to a failure of global climate cooperation."]},{"k":"p","s":["The science is clear: greenhouse gas emissions from coal, oil and gas are driving ",["climate change","https://www.un.org/en/climatechange/science/causes-effects-climate-change"],". With the world on track to “ ",["overshoot","https://www.unep.org/en/publications/report/limiting-overshoot-navigating-exceedance-15degc-and-pathways-towards-return"],"” the Paris Agreement ",["target of 1.5°C","https://theconversation.com/the-world-will-soon-shoot-past-1-5-c-what-does-this-mean-294577"],", reducing and ultimately eliminating fossil fuel use must be a priority."]},{"k":"p","s":["But there is still hope. While fossil fuels may be a source of discomfort for Australia and Turkey, this debate could spur global climate action in other ways."]},{"k":"p","s":["Introducing the global roadmap, for instance, could make the comparatively modest 35-by-35 electrification goal more appealing, particularly to countries that remain reluctant to phase out fossil fuels. This “decarbonisation by stealth” approach could help lower global emissions. However, some nations may support the electrification goal but ",["still resist","https://www.climatechangenews.com/2026/11/10/cop31-bulletin-day-2-energy-day-off-to-slow-start-amid-transport-chaos"]," calls to get that electricity from renewables. In that sense, failing to directly target fossil fuels may lead to partial or imperfect climate action."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nevertheless, expect the “F word” – fossil fuels – to remain centre stage during the second week of COP31 and future climate summits. We simply can’t afford to keep kicking this dirty can down the road."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Yes, the COP climate talks are far from perfect. But they still hold the power for change","https://theconversation.com/yes-the-cop-climate-talks-are-far-from-perfect-but-they-still-hold-the-power-for-change-295350"]]}],"chars":6027},"https://theconversation.com/rnzs-budget-crisis-threatens-its-core-purpose-but-theres-an-obvious-solution-296293":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"5d5d721794b2719e201c7a20787afa190246ae023b4a01ca69087311d938f7a7","read":"https://theconversation.com/rnzs-budget-crisis-threatens-its-core-purpose-but-theres-an-obvious-solution-296293","bytes":179439,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"RNZ’s budget crisis threatens its core purpose. But there’s an obvious solution","by":[{"n":"Peter Thompson","r":"Associate Professor in Media and Communication, Te Herenga Waka — Victoria University of Wellington"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T20:33:56Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["“News and information you can trust,” says the voiceover before each RNZ news bulletin. Unfortunately, it seems the same couldn’t be said for the state broadcaster’s internal accounting."]},{"k":"p","s":["RNZ’s ",["2025-26 annual report","https://www.rnz.co.nz/assets/cms_uploads/000/000/556/RNZ_2025-2026_Annual_Report_Web.pdf"],", released on November 9, revealed a NZ$11.8 million deficit – well in excess of the projected $470,000 loss in its earlier ",["statement of performance expectations","https://www.rnz.co.nz/assets/cms_uploads/000/000/506/2025-2026_Statement_of_Performance_Expectations.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The accounting discrepancy (now subject to an ",["independent review","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics/2491845/treasury-wants-own-oversight-of-rnz-to-be-part-of-independent-review"],") is a huge embarrassment for the RNZ board and executive team. The consequences for RNZ’s ability to fulfil its public service remit are potentially dire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Management and board were apparently unaware of the problem until the ",["sudden resignation of the chief financial officer","https://www.rnz.co.nz/national/programmes/checkpoint/audio/2019055120/rnz-chief-financial-officer-resigns-and-leaves-job-on-same-day"]," in early October."]},{"k":"p","s":["A subsequent ",["external audit of the accounts","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics/2491845/treasury-wants-own-oversight-of-rnz-to-be-part-of-independent-review"]," found multiple accounting errors relating to land sales, the Auckland office relocation, operational expenses, and personnel and redundancy costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["A $5 million loan facility was also found to have been set up without ministerial approval, ",["in breach of the Crown Entities Act","https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/rnzs-unlawful-overdraft-was-signed-off-by-the-board/HLTXAIVNAJGAHBOX7RO3WP2YJU/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["These anomalies raise serious questions about the integrity of RNZ’s financial governance, including the role of the board and its audit and risk committee. But the backdrop to the budget blowout is, if anything, of even greater concern."]},{"k":"h","s":["Huge workforce cuts"]},{"k":"p","s":["As ",["RNZ’s statement","https://www.rnz.co.nz/media/337"]," acknowledged, the errors were not picked up in time to take corrective action during the financial year, meaning “RNZ did not reduce its cost base as it needed to in response to a 7% reduction in baseline funding”."]},{"k":"p","s":["That refers to the government’s 2025 budget, which cut RNZ’s annual funding by $4.6 million a year, to $62.3 million – a reduction of $18.4 million over four years. The 2026 budget further reduced RNZ’s budget by $1.4 million."]},{"k":"p","s":["In response, RNZ had already ",["planned to cut 20 to 30 positions","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/2485692/rnz-blowout-big-cuts-big-hit-to-reputation"]," by mid-2027 ( ",["18 of which","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics/2487361/media-minister-rules-out-coming-to-rnz-s-aid-after-budget-blowout-a-colossal-mistake"]," had already been agreed through a voluntary process)."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the unexpected $11.8 million shortfall is now projected to mean the loss of 58 positions by next March – roughly 16% of the workforce – along with at least a 5% cut to operating expenditure."]},{"k":"p","s":["RNZ maintains it has adequate reserves to sustain it through a period of transition. But it projects a further $7.8 million deficit in the 2026-27 financial year, after which it will return to a sustainable footing."]},{"k":"p","s":["As board chair Brent Impey has indicated, the crisis is not an existential threat to RNZ: the $11.8 million deficit mainly ",["comprises one-off losses","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jVa24tVzkQw"],", including office relocation expenses and wrongly-accounted land sales."]},{"k":"p","s":["But if the board’s plan is to balance the books by the 2027-28 financial year, the concern is surely the impact this has on RNZ’s role as a public service media operation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political hostility"]},{"k":"p","s":["In contrast to its financial management, RNZ’s actual performance has been very positive."]},{"k":"p","s":["In line with its ",["letter of expectations","https://www.rnz.co.nz/assets/cms_uploads/000/000/538/RNZ_response_to_Minister_regarding_LoE_2026_-_28_April_2026.pdf"]," from shareholding ministers, it has increased its online and ",["linear","https://www.nzherald.co.nz/entertainment/linear-tv-overtakes-streaming-are-kiwis-tired-of-endless-choices/OUVW6MJM4NG6LGQKYITKCWK4BU/"]," audiences, reaching 83% of New Zealanders aged 18-plus each month. The 2026 ",["JMAD Trust in News report","https://www.jmadresearch.com/_files/ugd/a95e86_b1937c0c5f82498088e43cbb5552215d.pdf"]," ranked RNZ the most trusted New Zealand news source."]},{"k":"p","s":["RNZ also played a civil defence role in 26 emergencies. It shared news content with dozens of other news media (within New Zealand and in the Pacific), and supported the expansion of the ",["Local Democracy","https://www.rnz.co.nz/ldr"]," reporting scheme to 22 regional reporters."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to a survey quoted in its annual report, 79% of New Zealanders agreed it is important for the country to have a public media organisation."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this light, it’s also important the apparent failure of financial governance not be conflated with wider criticism of RNZ as an essential civic institution."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the latest budget shock has undoubtedly played into the hands of government politicians whose open hostility towards RNZ is well known."]},{"k":"p","s":["New Zealand First leader Winston Peters (at the time also deputy prime minister) directly ",["threatened the organisation’s funding","https://newsroom.co.nz/2025/06/25/the-many-hands-that-held-the-knife-against-rnz/"],". Meanwhile, ACT’s David Seymour (a shareholding minister of RNZ) criticised presenter appointments, alleged political bias and suggested cuts to RNZ’s budget. He also ",["called for an overhaul of the board","https://newsroom.co.nz/2026/05/08/hold-my-beer-seymour-takes-a-wild-swing-at-public-media/"]," and management."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tempting as it may be for RNZ’s ideological critics to point to recent financial failings as vindication of their concerns, it does not logically follow that RNZ’s performance as a public media operation is in question."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the contrary, what does merit review is the previous coalition government’s decision to repeatedly cut RNZ’s budget at the same time as demanding constant improvements in its programming performance."]},{"k":"h","s":["An obvious solution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Whatever the complexion of the new government, a bailout would likely be a politically untenable response to a crisis ostensibly of RNZ’s own making."]},{"k":"p","s":["But that is not necessary anyway. As Impey has noted, the sale of a transmitter site in Auckland is due to ",["bring in $51 million","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jVa24tVzkQw"]," in the next financial year. The only question is how much of this revenue RNZ will be permitted to retain by the Treasury."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even a quarter of that sum would be sufficient to offset the $11.8 million deficit. If that were permitted, there would be no need for additional redundancies and operational cost-cutting. RNZ could continue to deliver the services for which it is justifiably funded."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is therefore an obvious solution and a straightforward political decision to be made. But it will require the support of RNZ’s incoming shareholding ministers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regardless of which parties comprise the next government, they have a responsibility to ensure RNZ’s civic, democratic and cultural functions are not undermined."]}],"chars":5544},"https://theconversation.com/canada-can-develop-infrastructure-and-protect-biodiversity-293521":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"2f65e097dadbd2f8af9c388b0ee817775d19e3f3164e0d1a43237c34f3e594f2","read":"https://theconversation.com/canada-can-develop-infrastructure-and-protect-biodiversity-293521","bytes":189710,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Canada can develop infrastructure and protect biodiversity","by":[{"n":"Andrew Nicholas Kadykalo","r":"Adjunct Professor, School of Environment, Resources and Sustainability (SERS), University of Waterloo; Trent University"},{"n":"Elizabeth Ann Nyboer","r":"Assistant Professor, Department of Fish and Wildlife Conservation, Virginia Tech"},{"n":"Steven J Cooke","r":"Canada Research Professor, Conservation Physiology, Carleton University"}],"pub":"2026-11-01T13:08:02Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Nearly 200 countries recently came together in Armenia for the ",["2026 United Nations Biodiversity Conference","https://cop17yerevan.am/en"]," to review progress toward halting and reversing biodiversity loss. Many of these governments will soon convene again in Turkey to discuss ",["efforts to tackle climate change at COP31","https://unfccc.int/cop31"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, parties to the United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity adopted the ",["Kunming-Montréal Global Biodiversity Framework","https://www.cbd.int/gbf"]," aimed at reversing biodiversity loss by 2030 and put nature on a path to recovery by 2050. An early review of the first 36 national plans found that ",["none had created a plan that fully met two targets","https://theconversation.com/with-just-5-years-to-go-the-world-is-failing-on-a-vital-deal-to-halt-biodiversity-loss-249841"],": to restore 30 per cent of degraded ecosystems, and to conserve 30 per cent of lands and waters, by 2030."]},{"k":"p","s":["By the end of 2025, Canada had conserved ",["only 14 per cent of its land and fresh water and 15 per cent of its oceans","https://www.canada.ca/en/environment-climate-change/services/environmental-indicators/conserved-areas.html"],". In 2025, ",["the federal environment commissioner found","https://open.canada.ca/data/en/info/73a47fc9-d43b-480f-9eca-d83380f8e699"]," that the government ",["was not on track to meet its interim target of 25 per cent by 2025","https://www.canada.ca/en/auditor-general/media-room/canada-is-not-meeting-its-commitments-to-protect-and-conserve-land-and-inland-water.html"],", a target it went on to miss. A ",["companion audit","https://www.canada.ca/en/auditor-general/our-work/audit-reports/establishing-marine-protected-areas.html"]," reached the same conclusion for oceans."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a ",["party to the biodiversity convention","https://www.canada.ca/en/environment-climate-change/news/2022/12/canada-helps-lead-the-world-to-agreement-on-the-monumental-kunming-montreal-global-biodiversity-framework.html"],", Canada has a responsibility to conserve its ",["wilderness","https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-018-07183-6"],", ",["irrecoverable carbon","https://doi.org/10.1038/s41893-021-00803-6"],", ",["intact forests","https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.1600821"]," and ",["lakes","https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms13603"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the Canadian government is also pursuing infrastructure and resource development, with plans to fast-track approvals for major projects and build ",["“at speeds not seen in generations.”","https://www.canada.ca/en/privy-council/major-projects-office.html"]," It has also made ",["significant cuts to public science","https://evidencefordemocracy.ca/canada-is-cutting-public-science-the-risks-will-not-be-invisible-forever/"]," and faced criticism ",["over cuts to public engagement and consultation, as well as access to information","https://www.hilltimes.com/2026/08/03/the-canadian-government-is-cutting-out-meaningful-public-consultations-and-info-access/513412/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["We recently ",["published a study","https://doi.org/10.1002/2688-8319.70334"]," on how environmental research informs policy and practice through knowledge co-production. We interviewed 84 senior environmental professionals working at the science–policy interface across Canada, including federal, provincial and territorial governments and environmental non-profit organizations. We asked how environment-related evidence informs decisions and what enables or hinders knowledge co-production with a wide range of partners."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Budget cuts at Environment and Climate Change Canada threaten Arctic science","https://theconversation.com/budget-cuts-at-environment-and-climate-change-canada-threaten-arctic-science-276606"]]},{"k":"h","s":["What makes evidence count in policy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada faces a critical moment to show that rapid infrastructure growth does not have to come at the expense of nature and biodiversity goals. Doing so will require the deliberate use of the best available evidence to inform decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["It will also require inclusive, collaborative governance rooted in trust, early relationship-building and sustained co-operation among governments, academia, non-governmental organizations and Indigenous and local communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The biodiversity framework commits countries to ",["integrate biodiversity into decision-making at all levels","https://www.cbd.int/gbf/targets/14"],", ensure that access to the ",["best available data and knowledge guide action","https://www.cbd.int/gbf/targets/21"]," and guarantee inclusive, equitable ",["participation and representation in governance","https://www.cbd.int/gbf/targets/22"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The interviews we conducted predate the current push to fast-track major projects, but the barriers people described are the very ones that efforts to accelerate project approvals and development could make worse. This research, recently published, is especially relevant given Canada’s efforts to accelerate infrastructure development while meeting its environmental commitments."]},{"k":"p","s":["Interviewees told us that making information count in effective environmental policy depends on more than bringing people together. They pointed to building trust, jointly defining research questions, involving decision-makers and Knowledge Holders (including practitioners and Indigenous Peoples) early, and being transparent about how evidence is produced and interpreted."]},{"k":"p","s":["As one interviewee explained, when people are involved from the beginning, “even if the results are unexpected, they can say: ‘What you did made sense.’” Another interviewee similarly noted that knowledge co-production “shortens the path to use” by involving those who need or can benefit from the knowledge in its production from the outset."]},{"k":"p","s":["Trust, respect and recognition were the most frequently mentioned themes associated with successful knowledge co-production and evidence-based conservation in our study, followed by funding and resources."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["new global review of research on evidence use in conservation","https://besjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/1365-2664.70565"]," found a similar pattern, where relationships developed among scientists and decision-makers, the relevance of evidence, and the capacity and resources of organizations were the most frequently reported to influence evidence use."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings highlight the importance of ",["early relationship-building, shared goals, clear communication and sustained cross-sector collaboration","https://doi.org/10.1002/2688-8319.70334"]," — all of which require time and ",["institutional support","https://doi.org/10.3389/fcosc.2021.693129"],". The barriers that the people we interviewed raised most often were the opposite, including tight budgets and limited staff time."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet these are precisely the conditions that can be undermined when governments fast-track projects while reducing scientific capacity, public engagement and consultation."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a ",["companion paper based on the same suite of interviews","https://doi.org/10.1111/csp2.426"],", we outlined how evidence syntheses — research that critically reviews, collates and summarizes available knowledge — can increase confidence in the evidence and resulting decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also found that understandings of ",["what counts as evidence are shifting","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envsci.2025.104176"],". Decision-makers are increasingly looking to draw on diverse forms of evidence, but considerable uncertainty remains about how best to bring them together in a respectful and meaningful way."]},{"k":"h","s":["What knowledge co-production brings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet there is growing recognition that diverse evidence ",["does not always translate into its use","https://doi.org/10.1002/pan3.10194"],". Most environmental professionals we interviewed still viewed peer-reviewed natural science ",["as the gold standard","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envsci.2025.104176"],". Indigenous, local and community knowledge, and social science, were frequently discussed but tended to be neglected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indigenous knowledge was the form of evidence interviewees most often said they were not using. Many wanted to draw on it but lacked the know-how, capacity or time to do so. Others noted that mandates to include Indigenous knowledge often came without practical guidance."]},{"k":"p","s":["This matters when decisions are fast-tracked. Interviewees told us that short timelines already keep harder-to-access forms of evidence out of decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under even tighter timelines, environmental evidence may be overlooked entirely, or decision-makers may rely on what is most readily available: in-house science and familiar experts. This can favour perspectives already represented while sidelining other relevant evidence and knowledge held by those most affected, including Indigenous rights-holders and local communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Knowledge co-production offers one way to address this imbalance. Knowledge co-production means developing knowledge alongside those who will use it. Rather than working in isolation and sharing findings at the end, researchers collaborate with governments, Indigenous organizations, communities, industry and other partners from the outset to shape research questions, interpret evidence and apply findings to real-world challenges."]},{"k":"p","s":["By involving partners from the outset, decision-makers and knowledge holders can jointly identify the questions that matter, determine which forms of evidence are needed, and discuss how different knowledge systems can inform decisions. Rather than retrofitting Indigenous and/or local knowledge to support predetermined decisions, knowledge co-production creates space to consider them meaningfully from the beginning."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada can pursue ambitious social and economic goals while meeting its environmental commitments. Success will ",["require evidence-informed decisions that respect Indigenous rights, are legally sound and work in practice","https://theconversation.com/elbows-up-in-canada-means-sustainable-resource-development-255669"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our research shows that trust, early relationship-building and sustained collaboration help deliver durable decisions without unnecessary barriers to development. Efforts to accelerate decision-making should not come at the expense of these foundations."]}],"chars":7956},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guinea":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"9caf778143692aa0afad3fad9a660efda14fc5eea35023d20e2c816a0310c8ca","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/guinea","bytes":58677,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Guinea travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-10T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-12T16:34:39+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guinea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Guinea’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Guinea set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Guinean Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Guinea, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Guinea for up to 90 days. Make sure you apply for the correct visa – British nationals have been refused entry with the wrong one."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["apply online for an e-visa for private and business travel","https://www.paf.gov.gn/visa"],". You must apply several days in advance and upload scanned documents, including a yellow fever vaccination certificate. When you arrive in Guinea, take your e-visa registration receipt to the entry checkpoint, where border officials will issue your visa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Guinea, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, including yellow fever, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Guinea guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/97/guinea#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Guinea. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Guinea"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no limit on cash you can bring into Guinea. When you leave, you cannot take more than 100,000 Guinean francs, or 5,000 US dollars or the equivalent in euros."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Guinea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Guinea cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreigners. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["While the political environment is currently stable, there is ongoing tension between the government and opposition parties."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests linked to economic challenges, such as electricity shortages, occur from time to time. Tensions can rise quickly. Public gatherings and demonstrations can start with little or no warning and may turn violent. In the past, protestors have damaged public buildings, and there have been fatalities and injuries among protestors and bystanders."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay away from demonstrations, especially near military installations, and monitor reliable, local and international media for updates. If you see crowds forming or signs of unrest, move promptly to a safe location."]},{"k":"h","s":["Security situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Border areas of Guinea are often tense with an increased military presence. Security has improved but things can still be tense, particularly at big events such as elections."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["For assistance or to report a crime in Conakry, call the local police Commissaire on +224 622 86 94 71."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals posing as police or military, armed with military weapons, have robbed drivers and their passengers at gunpoint, particularly at night. Violent carjackings are a threat, especially in the outlying suburbs of Conakry. Reduce the risk of vehicle crime by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["getting security advice before travelling by road"]},{"k":"li","s":["travelling in convoy"]},{"k":"li","s":["using reputable travel operators and taxis, arranged in advance"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping doors locked and windows closed while driving"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional reports of hold-ups and armed robbery on the roads to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mamou"]},{"k":"li","s":["Faranah"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kissidougou"]},{"k":"li","s":["Guékédou"]},{"k":"li","s":["Macenta"]},{"k":"li","s":["N’zérékoré"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to arrive in Conakry on a flight after dark, arrange your airport transfer before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your possessions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Break-ins are common, and burglars may be armed. There is also a high level of street crime – mugging, pickpocketing and bag-snatching. Take precautions by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ensuring your accommodation is secure and has security guards"]},{"k":"li","s":["taking a pre-arranged taxi if you are changing money or visiting a bank"]},{"k":"li","s":["not wearing expensive-looking jewellery or watches and keeping mobiles out of sight"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoiding emptier parts of towns and cities"]},{"k":"li","s":["not walking alone at night"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams and extortion"]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy in Conakry is aware of police extorting cash from foreigners and Guineans."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care if you trade gold and diamonds. This trade attracts criminal gangs and can involve kidnapping and extortion. There are reports of trading scams involving diamonds, gold export and gold certification."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Detention"]},{"k":"p","s":["The criminal justice process in Guinea falls below international standards. If you are arrested or detained due process may not be followed and delays should be expected. Pre-trial detention is common and can last for many months."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local prison conditions are harsh, often without regular food and water. The main prison in Conakry suffers from serious overcrowding."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry photo ID such as a passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not become involved with illegal drugs of any kind."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you commit a drugs crime, you are likely to be prosecuted. There are heavy penalties for those convicted."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photography and filming in many areas is highly restricted. This includes:"]},{"k":"li","s":["military bases and checkpoints"]},{"k":"li","s":["the President’s residence and offices"]},{"k":"li","s":["police and gendarmerie HQs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to photograph or film anything of strategic value such as airports and bridges. Do not photograph military or police installations or government buildings, or you could be arrested."]},{"k":"p","s":["Individuals may prefer not to be photographed. If in doubt, ask, or do not take pictures."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit cards are not widely used in Guinea and obtaining hard currency is very difficult. There are a few ATMs in Conakry that accept foreign cards, but they give only small amounts of currency. They are also unreliable. Banks in Conakry accept international credit cards and exchange money."]},{"k":"p","s":["Exchanging foreign currency on the street is illegal. Foreign nationals have been arrested and held in military custody for using unofficial money changers even for small amounts, including at the airport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal. Penalties range from 6 months to 3 years in prison and a fine of 500,000 to 1 million Guinean francs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are not widely accepted or understood. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Precious stones"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need an export licence to take precious stones out of Guinea. Gem smuggling is illegal, and anyone convicted can expect a severe prison sentence. Local prison conditions are harsh."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Guinea, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most major hotels and travel agencies offer cars for hire, with a driver if required."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road travel can be hazardous, especially during the rainy season from May to October. Roads, even within Conakry and other principal towns, can be flooded and become impassable."]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of road maintenance is low. Many roads are unmetalled and have deep potholes as damage caused during the rainy season goes unrepaired."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fuel is not always available at petrol stations. Carry an emergency supply on long journeys."]},{"k":"p","s":["British Embassy staff avoid road travel outside the Conakry region at night. If staff choose to hire transport for personal journeys, they are encouraged to satisfy themselves in advance of the vehicle’s roadworthiness and the driver’s competence. The use of moto-taxis and shared taxis/tuk-tuks is not advised."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buses and taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis and long-distance buses are generally poorly maintained, overcrowded, and the drivers are often unqualified."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Roadblocks and checkpoints"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police and local militia maintain checkpoints across the country. They check vehicle and passenger documentation and baggage. Corruption and extortion are common at roadblocks. Occasionally, checkpoints can be a pretext for armed robbery."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities may close the Guinea-Sierra Leone border at short notice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of piracy attacks against vessels in Guinean territorial waters."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical numbers"]},{"k":"p","s":["In remote areas you will have to arrange local transport. In Conakry, call local clinics."]},{"k":"p","s":["Clinique Pasteur: +224 621 35 01 01 or +224 664 26 98 53"]},{"k":"p","s":["International Clinic: +224 654 05 55 55 or +224 654 09 99 99"]},{"k":"p","s":["Clinique Ambroise Paré: +224 631 40 10 40"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hôpital de l’Amitié Sino-Guinéenne: +224 621 08 88 62"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Guinea","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/97/guinea#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Guinea","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/97/guinea"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional outbreaks of Ebola in Guinea. The last one was in 2021. Cholera and malaria are also present in Guinea and have similar early symptoms to Ebola. You can read ",["more information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/68/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are some well-stocked pharmacies in Conakry but few outside the capital. Check that medicine is genuine."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Guinea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are poor. Equipment is basic and often not sterile. Carry basic medical supplies and a first aid kit."]},{"k":"p","s":["For serious medical treatment, medical evacuation to Europe is necessary. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Guinea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/guinea-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Guinea"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no emergency services in Guinea. If you need urgent medical assistance, contact a clinic in Conakry:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Clinique Pasteur: +224 621 35 01 01 or +224 664 26 98 53"]},{"k":"p","s":["Clinique Ambroise Paré: +224 631 40 10 40"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Guinea"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Guinea"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Guinea"]," in Guinea"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Guinea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/guinea-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Guinea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/guinea-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guinea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also ",["contact FCDO online","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/guinea/british-embassy-conakry"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad in an emergency"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Guinea and you need emergency help from the UK government, contact the ",["British Embassy in Conakry","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-conakry"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy in Conakry can only provide limited emergency consular assistance. Access to the Embassy is strictly by appointment only. Please send an email to BritishEmbassy.Conakry@fcdo.gov.uk for consular assistance or to make an appointment. If you need urgent consular help, call +44 (0) 1908 516 666."]},{"k":"hs","s":["FCDO in London"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Guinea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-guinea"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":14594,"change":"Updated information about health risks you’ll face in Guinea (‘Health’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"76e1af6c3887c812e60969ffa374095e2ddb24b937787fd416f06d3303947dcd","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/india","bytes":123200,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"India travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T15:39:35+00:00","mod":"2026-10-07T11:56:27+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["India-Pakistan border area"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 10km of the India-Pakistan border, except for Wagah-Attari border crossing. While The Wagah-Attari border crossing is currently closed, visitors can still access and attend the daily border retreat ceremony."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir (including Pahalgam, Gulmarg, Sonamarg, the city of Srinagar and the Jammu-Srinagar national highway), except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel by air to and from the city of Jammu"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel within the city of Jammu"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Manipur"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Manipur including the capital, Imphal. Curfews and restrictions continue in parts of Manipur following ongoing ethnic violence since May 2023."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel to these regions","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"li","s":["If you have been impacted by travel disruption and need to review your Indian visa contact the nearest Foreigners Regional Registration Office (FRRO). See ",["e-FRRO Home","https://indianfrro.gov.in/eservices/"]," (website not accessible outside India)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of India’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in India set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["High Commission of India in London","https://www.hcilondon.gov.in/"]," or ",["another Indian consulate","https://www.hcilondon.gov.in/page/consular-jurisdiction/"]," in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter India, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and have at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport if you need to","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Returning to the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, ",["British citizens","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"]," must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit India unless you are an Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) cardholder."]},{"k":"p","s":["India has a number of visa categories including tourist, business, work, journalist and medical. Make sure you get the right visa for your travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You could be refused entry or deported for having the wrong visa. You could also be banned from entering India in the future."]},{"k":"p","s":["For the latest information on Indian visas and immigration requirements, see the ",["Indian Bureau of Immigration","https://boi.gov.in/boi/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa or e-visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out how to apply for a visa from the ",["Indian Bureau of Immigration","https://boi.gov.in/boi/"],". Depending on your requirements, you may be able to apply for a:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["regular (paper) visa","https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/visa/index.html"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["e-visa","https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/evisa/tvoa.html"]," (check the website’s FAQs for restrictions on airports, land borders and seaports of entry)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check your eligibility and any restrictions before you apply. Allow plenty of time for your application to be processed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applicants of Pakistani origin"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are of Pakistani origin, a British-Pakistani dual national or hold a National Identity Card for Overseas Pakistanis (NICOP), the visa processing time will be substantially longer than other visa applications. More information is available from the ",["High Commission of India","https://www.hcilondon.gov.in/page/persons-of-pakistani-origin/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British-Pakistani dual national, you must apply for an Indian visa on your Pakistani passport. If you have renounced your Pakistani nationality, or cancelled your Pakistani passport, you will need to submit documentary proof of this."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) cardholders"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hold a valid Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) card, you can use this, along with your valid British passport, to visit India. You do not need a visa. An Electronic Overseas Citizen of India (e-OCI) was launched in June 2026 and means holders of an e-OCI card need not carry a physical copy of the card. More information is available at ",["Online OCI Services","https://ociservices.gov.in/onlineOCI/"],", including the requirement for special permission to undertake certain activities such as research, missionary activities or journalism."]},{"k":"hs","s":["E-arrival card"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals arriving in India must complete an ",["e-arrival card","https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/earrival/"]," online before reaching immigration. The online e-arrival card can be completed up to 72 hours before you arrive. You should complete the online process in advance to avoid delays at the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["More details are available on the ",["Indian visa website","https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/"],". The e-arrival card is not a visa, and you will still need a separate valid visa or OCI card to enter India."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extending your visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to overstay your visa in India. Make sure you leave the country before your visa expires or get an extension if permitted to do so. More information is available from the ",["Indian Bureau of Immigration","https://boi.gov.in/boi/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["If you’re hospitalised"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you or someone you’re travelling with has a short-term tourist visa and is hospitalised, you may be able to ",["convert to a medical visa","https://boi.gov.in/boi/contents/registration-authority/miscellaneous-services/medical-exigency"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure the border control officer puts a stamp in your passport when you arrive in India. You’ll need to show it when you leave, so border control officers know you have not overstayed your visa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hotels, hostels and other accommodation providers must register foreign guests with the ",["Foreigners Regional Registration Office","https://indianfrro.gov.in/efrro/home"],". Make sure your accommodation provider, for example, hotels, hostels and homestead owners, registers you ",["using the online C-form","https://indianfrro.gov.in/frro/FormC"],". (Web pages not accessible outside India)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need your passport with a valid visa to get accommodation in country. British nationals who have overstayed their Indian visa have found it difficult to find accommodation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to stay in India for more than 180 days and do not hold an OCI card, you must register within 14 days of arrival with the ",["Foreigners Regional Registration Office","https://indianfrro.gov.in/efrro/home"]," (website not accessible outside India). You could be denied permission to leave if you do not do this."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need to register your stay depending on the type of visa you hold, check if you need to."]},{"k":"h","s":["Exit requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["When you leave India, officials will check when you entered the country. If you do not have an entry stamp, for example, if you have a newly issued passport or an emergency travel document, you must ",["apply for a special exit permit before you travel","https://boi.gov.in/boi/contents/travelling-abroad/foreigners/general-information"],". If you need to apply for an exit permit, you can only apply to the ",["Foreigners Regional Registration Office","https://indianfrro.gov.in/"]," from within India (website not accessible outside India). It can take between 5 and 15 working days for straightforward applications. Factor this into your timeframe to leave India when you are booking flights."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter India, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["polio vaccine if you’re coming from a polio-affected country"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s India guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/105/india#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a public health measure, India has introduced health screening measures, including completing a mandatory Self-Declaration Form for all international passengers arriving in India. The Self-Declaration Form should be completed up to 24 hours before arrival through the ",["Air Suvidha Portal.","https://airsuvidha.civilaviation.gov.in/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you don’t complete the form before you arrive, expect delays. Travellers from affected regions should also be prepared to undertake temperature checks. If you show symptoms, you may be subject to isolation, quarantine, and/or travel restrictions. Monitor local media and follow the advice of the airlines you are travelling with, local authorities and your travel company."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of India","https://www.cbic.gov.in/entities/internationalTravellers"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into India"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are restrictions on bringing Indian rupees into India. Visitors, including residents and tourists, must follow ",["Reserve Bank of India guidelines","https://m.rbi.org.in/scripts/FAQView.aspx?Id=66#q4"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting India, you can bring cash, travellers cheques (in British pounds or another foreign currency) or a bank card with you and exchange or withdraw rupees in India."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare any amount above 5,000 US dollars in notes, or 10,000 US dollars in notes and travellers cheques combined."]},{"k":"h","s":["Access permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["Special permits are required to visit certain parts of India designated as restricted or protected areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Permit regulations can change at any time."]},{"k":"p","s":["Information is available from:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the ",["Ministry of Home Affairs","https://www.mha.gov.in/sites/default/files/2022-08/AnnexVII_01022018%5B1%5D.pdf"]," website"]},{"k":"li","s":["local tour operators"]},{"k":"li","s":["the relevant state liaison office"]},{"k":"li","s":["the ",["Indian Bureau of Immigration","https://boi.gov.in/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["You need to apply for permits 3 months before your arrival. You can submit your application:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the UK, to the ",["High Commission of India in London","https://www.hcilondon.gov.in/"]," or ",["another Indian consulate","https://www.hcilondon.gov.in/page/consular-jurisdiction/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["in India, to the liaison office of the state for which you need a permit or the ",["Foreigners Regional Registration Office (FRRO)","https://indianfrro.gov.in/efrro/home"]," (website not accessible outside India)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign tourists and researchers must keep to security and administrative guidelines during visits to tribal areas across the country. For the more information see the ",["Indian Bureau of Immigration","https://boi.gov.in/boi/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of India","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in India."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened risk of terrorism in some Indian regions. Read ",["our advice on regional risks in India","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india/regional-risks"]," for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist and insurgent groups operating in India include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lashkar-e-Taiba (LeT), Jaish-e-Mohammed (JeM) and associated proxy groups such as The Resistance Front in Indian-administered Kashmir"]},{"k":"li","s":["Naxalite (Maoist or Left Wing Extremism) groups active in some of the India’s eastern, southern and central states"]},{"k":"li","s":["Khalistani extremists operating mainly in Punjab"]},{"k":"li","s":["Daesh, Al Qa’ida in the Indian Subcontinent (AQIS) and other groups may also be planning attacks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks have targeted Indian government interests and civilians, including tourists and foreign nationals. Security has been strengthened, including at major hotels and transport hubs. However, terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["restaurants, hotels, bars, shopping centres and markets"]},{"k":"li","s":["stations and airports"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship and tourist attractions"]},{"k":"li","s":["festivals, sports venues and beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care during periods of national or religious significance, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Republic Day (26 January)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Independence Day (15 August)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Diwali (usually in October or November)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Eid (date changes each year)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings and keep up to date with local media reports. It is advisable to always carry identity documents and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Demonstrations and mass gatherings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Strikes (sometimes referred to as ‘bandh’ or ‘hartal’), political rallies and demonstrations happen frequently and can become violent. The risks are higher during elections and after the death of party or government leaders. Protests can happen at short notice, especially around days of national importance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local authorities may impose curfews and other restrictions. Transport and public services including mobile networks and internet may be disrupted. Stampedes have occurred during some events with large crowds like sporting events, parades or religious gatherings resulting in death and injuries."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid protests or demonstrations, rallies and large gatherings including at religious sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of the local authorities and your travel company"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media and follow any curfew restrictions"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re the victim of crime in India, call:"]},{"k":"li","s":["police helpline: 100"]},{"k":"li","s":["national emergency number: 112"]},{"k":"li","s":["women helpline: 1091"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep a copy of your passport complete with your emergency contact details, visa and flight ticket separately from originals when travelling. Leave copies at home where others can access them, and store copies electronically. If your passport is lost or stolen, tell the police immediately and get a police report. You will need the police report for your exit visa application."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care of your possessions on buses, trains and in crowds. Criminals may ride past on motorbikes and snatch valuables."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious in tourist areas, where scammers, pickpockets and ticket touts target foreign nationals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cybercrime, internet scamming, card skimming and confidence scams are common. These scams come in many forms and can cause great financial loss."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals often use the details of British High Commissions and Embassies. Be cautious and check the authenticity of details before responding."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a victim, report it to local police and obtain a copy of the report for your insurer. You can also report a cybercrime on the National Cybercrime Helpline by dialling 1930 and make a complaint on the ",["national portal","https://cybercrime.gov.in/Default.aspx"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink and food spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be wary of accepting drinks or food from strangers or leaving drinks unattended. There have been reports of spiked drinks and food, with British nationals being robbed or assaulted."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and Methanol Poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of sexual assault, including attacks on female foreign national visitors in tourist areas and cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Female travellers often experience verbal and physical harassment by individuals or groups of men. Serious sexual attacks involving both Indian and foreign nationals have been reported. British women have been victims of sexual assault, including rape, in multiple states in India. Avoid isolated areas, including beaches, when alone at any time of day."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad."],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Respect local dress code and customs, particularly when visiting religious sites and rural areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Laws on alcohol, including buying, drinking and the legal drinking age, vary by state. Get advice from your travel agent, hotel or the authorities about the laws in areas you are visiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol in public places, such as parks."]},{"k":"p","s":["In some states, foreign nationals and non-resident Indians can buy 30-day alcohol permits."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is often a ban on the sale of alcohol during major religious festivals, national holidays and elections. Police can carry out vehicle checks during this period."]},{"k":"p","s":["The consumption, production or transportation of alcohol is illegal in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bihar"]},{"k":"li","s":["Gujarat"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mizoram"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nagaland"]},{"k":"li","s":["Union Territory of Lakshadweep"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you drink or possess alcohol in these states, you could be arrested and held without bail. You could face a prison sentence of 5 to 10 years."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and vapes bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke in most public places. Only smoke in designated smoking areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vapes and related products are banned. You cannot buy vapes in India or bring them into the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not get involved with any illegal drugs. Drugs are not categorised as they would be in the UK, into Class A, B and C and possession of any illegal drug could lead to sentencing. You could face a minimum sentence of 6 months for possession of small amounts deemed for personal consumption only, up to a 10-year sentence for other amounts. The judicial process is slow, and you could be detained for several years while your case is processed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Activities involving cameras and binoculars, like photography, birdwatching or plane spotting, may be misunderstood. Be particularly careful near military sites, government buildings, airports and railway stations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Satellite phones and other devices"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess and operate satellite phones and GPS devices in India without a licence, even if you are only transiting through India. This may also cover other satellite-enabled devices, including handheld or cycling GPSs. You can be fined or arrested for possession of these devices without permission and the item can be confiscated."]},{"k":"p","s":["A number of British nationals have been arrested or detained for bringing satellite phones and other satellite-enabled navigational devices into the country without prior permission. Contact the Indian Department of Telecommunication to ",["request a licence","https://dot.gov.in/contact-us"],". Further information is also available at the ",["Bureau of Civil Aviation Security","https://bcasindia.gov.in/#/pages/permitted-and-prohibited/electronic-items"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strong currents in rivers and off many coasts and people drown every year. Most beaches do not have warning signs, flags or lifesaving equipment. Take local advice and follow warnings and instructions issued by lifeguards. Emergency service standards may differ from those in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Trekking in India"]},{"k":"p","s":["Trekkers should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel in groups"]},{"k":"li","s":["use reputable local guides and stay on established routes"]},{"k":"li","s":["check if you need any special permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["Leave details of where you’re going and when you expect to return with your accommodation. You are extremely unlikely to have a phone signal in the mountains, so make sure your accommodation provider registers your whereabouts using the ",["online C-form","https://indianfrro.gov.in/frro/FormC"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess or operate satellite phones or GPS devices without prior permission of the Indian authorities. ",["Contact the Indian Department of Telecommunication to request a licence","https://dot.gov.in/contact-us"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hazards when trekking exist throughout the year, especially above 3,000 metres, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["altitude sickness"]},{"k":"li","s":["sudden weather changes, including thunderstorms"]},{"k":"li","s":["avalanches and snow drifts"]},{"k":"li","s":["landslides, flooding and rock falls"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your insurance policy covers you for altitudes over 2,400m and mountain rescue and helicopter costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["While commercial ground-based search and rescue (SAR) teams generally do not operate at base stations above 3,000m, commercial helicopters do. This would require insurance. In some border areas only the Indian Air Force can carry out air rescues. However, they are under no obligation to perform them and only carry out rescues during working hours."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual relationships are legal in India. However same-sex marriage is illegal. Indian society is conservative. This includes attitudes to LGBT+ people, which can be less accepting than in the UK. There is a risk of harassment and discrimination, especially outside of big cities. Showing affection in public may attract unwanted and negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Child custody and family law"]},{"k":"p","s":["Indian family law is different from UK law. Special caution is needed when child custody becomes an issue. In case of dispute, ",["consult a lawyer in India","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=India"]," to find out more about the relevant laws."]},{"k":"p","s":["Commercial surrogacy is illegal for foreign nationals in India. Overseas Citizens of India (OCI) should seek legal guidance on non-commercial (altruistic) surrogacy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade its parts without a licence. India has a strong legal framework to regulate and restrict wildlife trade and is also a signatory to the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES). If you’re caught purchasing or trafficking these illegally, you will be prosecuted and receive a prison sentence or fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual offences against children"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for any form of sexual offence against a child. There is a minimum jail term of 20 years, which may go up to life in prison or a death sentence, for anyone convicted of raping a child aged 12 or under."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving in India"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in India, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rules on how long you can drive on a UK licence vary from state to state."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["India has a high death rate from road accidents. Comply with the police if they are at the scene. If the police are not present, it could be unsafe to remain at the scene. If safe to do so, go to the nearest police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving can be dangerous in urban and rural areas due to wandering livestock. Accidents involving cows can draw crowds and potentially lead to violence. Anyone in the vehicle involved may be attacked or targeted for extortion. It is common to use your horn or flash your headlights frequently to announce your presence on the road."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid travelling at night and in fog as accidents are common due to low visibility and there is a higher risk of crime at night. Always travel in a well-maintained vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel by motorbike, wear a helmet and proper footwear."]},{"k":"p","s":["Buses are often driven fast and recklessly. Accidents are common."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful when crossing streets, even in marked pedestrian areas and especially at night, as vehicles sometimes drive on the wrong side of the road."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis and rickshaws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid travelling alone and hailing taxis on the street, especially at night. App-based taxis like Uber and Ola are widely available, including in all airport terminal buildings. Pre-paid taxi services are also available and many hotels offer transfers. If a hotel driver is collecting you at the airport by, make sure they properly identify themselves before you set off."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you book a taxi online, there’s usually a way to share journey details with your contacts who can then follow your location."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seatbelts are not common in 3-wheel taxis (autos) or in the back seats of taxis. Try to use taxis that have seatbelts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling through an airport, allow enough time to complete check-in and security procedures, as your baggage may need to go through screening equipment and checks. Allow time for transiting between flights if you need to change from international terminals to domestic terminals, even if using the airport shuttle service. Some places, e.g. Mumbai and Goa, have two airports located at a considerable distance from each other. Check your airport when booking your flights, especially if you are transiting through these places."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive on a charter flight booked through a tour operator, you can only fly into and out of the country with the same charter operator. Chartered flight passengers are not allowed to fly into or out of the country using a scheduled airline."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Train travel in India is generally safe, however accidents happen and have previously resulted in death and serious injury. There are police or guards on trains and stations if you need help. You must carry valid ID."]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling by train:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not accept food or drinks from strangers"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care of your passport and valuables as thefts are common"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid people at railway stations offering tickets and tours as you may be scammed"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourist boats and other small craft rarely carry life-saving equipment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although piracy has not so far affected India’s territorial waters, it poses a significant threat in parts of the Indian Ocean. Mariners should follow shipping industry guidelines on precautions to take."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ships and crew must have the necessary authorisation and paperwork before entering Indian territorial waters and follow Indian laws and regulations. If carrying weapons on board ships in Indian territorial waters, you must follow Indian laws and regulations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["India can experience extreme weather events that threaten life and disrupt infrastructure, including buildings, roads and communications."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["plan your travel so that you are aware of seasonal weather events, such as monsoon rains"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities and your travel company"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the ",["Indian Meteorological Department","https://mausam.imd.gov.in/"]," for weather updates"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Monsoons"]},{"k":"p","s":["The monsoon season in India usually runs from June to November. Monsoon rains can cause:"]},{"k":"li","s":["flash flooding and landslides, which can often occur with limited warning, sometimes leading to significant loss of life and property, particularly in mountainous areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["towns and villages to be cut off"]},{"k":"li","s":["road closures affecting transport links"]},{"k":"li","s":["disruption in big cities due to flooding"]},{"k":"li","s":["disruption to services including telephone lines, internet services and electricity"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cyclones and tropical storms"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones are a risk in India, particularly in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the east coast of India, from September to December"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Bay of Bengal, from April to June and September to December"]},{"k":"li","s":["south India, from June to November"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones can cause:"]},{"k":"li","s":["high winds: buildings can be damaged or destroyed; trees, power and telephone lines fall; flying debris becomes dangerous"]},{"k":"li","s":["storm surges: a tropical cyclone can cause a temporary rise in sea level of several metres which can flood coastal areas and damage buildings on the shoreline"]},{"k":"li","s":["very heavy rainfall: this can cause localised or widespread flooding and mudslides"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Several parts of India lie on highly active fault zones, including areas of the north and north-east. The most active are along the length of the Himalayas. Tremors are common in these regions and can cause landslides. Limited emergency response vehicles, equipment and medical facilities could increase an earthquake’s impact."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of India. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india/safety-and-security"]," for India."]},{"k":"h","s":["India-Pakistan border area and western India"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 10km of the India-Pakistan border. The Wagah-Attari border crossing is closed for tourist transit except for the daily border retreat ceremony. If you have plans to travel to India from Pakistan using any land borders, make alternate plans and follow the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["The India-Pakistan border in Gujarat and Rajasthan is unmarked in some areas. Approaching it away from an official crossing point could be dangerous. Where it is unmarked, you could enter Pakistan illegally."]},{"k":"h","s":["Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir (including Pahalgam, Gulmarg, Sonamarg, the city of Srinagar and the Jammu-Srinagar national highway), except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel by air to and from the city of Jammu"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel within the city of Jammu"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been frequent terrorist incidents in Jammu and Kashmir. There is a continuing threat, towards Indian government targets and civilians including tourists and foreign nationals. See ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heavy security presence in the Kashmir Valley. This, combined with violent protests and operations by security forces, has resulted in a number of deaths and serious casualties."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities can impose and lift curfews and other restrictions frequently and quickly. Stay vigilant, monitor local media, and follow the advice of local authorities and your travel company."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals are vulnerable in rural districts and outside the main population centres and tourist areas. There is a risk of unpredictable violence, including bombings, grenade attacks, shootings and kidnapping. The long-standing policy of the UK government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The level of consular assistance that the ",["British High Commission in India","https://www.gov.uk/government/world/organisations/british-high-commission-new-delhi"]," can provide in Jammu and Kashmir is severely limited."]},{"k":"h","s":["Manipur"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Manipur due to ongoing ethnic violence since May 2023."]},{"k":"p","s":["There may be curfews and other restrictions including transport disruptions and the suspension of internet services at short notice in some parts of the state."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some insurgent groups are active in north-east India including in the state of Manipur."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid protests or large gatherings"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of the local authorities and your travel company"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media and follow any curfew restrictions"]},{"k":"h","s":["Other north-eastern states"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sudden flareups and skirmishes may happen along inter-state borders in north-east India including Assam-Meghalaya borders. Please check with local authorities before traveling in the region."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been skirmishes on the India-Bangladesh border. Travellers are advised to check with local authorities that it is safe to travel before visiting these areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests, blockades and large gatherings are common in India’s north-eastern states. They can happen without warning and occasionally result in disorder. Blockades and protests may disrupt traffic along the national highways connecting them with each other and with Assam."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid protests and leave as soon as possible if a crowd develops. Review your security arrangements carefully and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, Odisha, Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra"]},{"k":"p","s":["Naxalite (Maoist or Left Wing Extremism) insurgents target police officers, paramilitary forces and government officials leading to injuries and deaths. Seek advice from your travel provider and local authorities on LWE-affected areas if you plan to travel to these states. ",["Ministry of Home Affairs","https://www.mha.gov.in/en/divisionofmha/left-wing-extremism-division"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Goa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Opportunistic criminals operate in Goa because of the high number of tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been some serious incidents involving British nationals in recent years, including sexual assaults."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol in public places in Goa. If you drink alcohol outside the limits of a licensed premises, you could be fined or given a prison sentence. You can drink within the limits of a registered beach shack or bar, for example, but not on an open beach or road."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for India","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/countries/india#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what health risks you’ll face in India, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue and malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"li","s":["poor air quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts India. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air pollution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Severe air pollution is a major health hazard, especially during the winter months from October to February. North Indian cities and metros across the country are most affected by extremely high levels of pollution. Children, the elderly and those with pre-existing medical conditions may be especially affected. If you’re pregnant or have a respiratory or heart condition you may wish to consult a medical practitioner before you travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies are widely available in India. Most medicines that require a prescription in the UK will require one in India. Take your existing medicine packaging to show them exactly what you need."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in India"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities differ from those in the UK, especially in more remote areas. Specialised treatment may not be available outside major cities. In major cities, government and more expensive private medical care is available."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in India","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/india-list-of-hospitals"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hospitals in India usually ask for a guardian or an attendant to stay in the hospital with the patient. It is possible to find agencies who will provide a caregiver for a fee, but it may be difficult to find someone who speaks English. If you know you need hospital care in India, you should try and organise a guardian such as a friend or relative who can stay with you for the duration."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transplant surgery"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to India for organ transplant surgery, check in advance with the hospital what proof they need about your circumstances in the UK. You may need to submit evidence of your marriage and birth of your children before the operation can take place. You can get copies of marriage and birth certificates from the ",["General Register Office in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/general-register-office"],". You may want to ",["get your documents legalised","https://www.gov.uk/get-document-legalised"]," before travelling. The British High Commission cannot provide guarantees and certificates on your behalf."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are considering travelling to India for medical treatment:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read more advice on ",["going abroad for medical treatment and elective surgery","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["discuss plans with your UK doctor before going ahead with any medical procedures abroad"]},{"k":"li","s":["do your own research – private companies have a financial interest in arranging your medical treatment abroad and the information they provide should not be your only source of information"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find further ",["advice on medical tourism from TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/59/medical-tourism-travelling-for-treatment"]," and NHS guidance on ",["going abroad for medical treatment","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/going-abroad-for-treatment/going-abroad-for-medical-treatment/"]," and ",["cosmetic surgery abroad","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/cosmetic-procedures/advice/cosmetic-surgery-abroad/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency services in India"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["These services provide support in English, Hindi and additional languages."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also download the 112 India mobile app which can track your location to support response in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Further helpline numbers are available on the [National Portal of India.] (https://www.india.gov.in/directory/helpline))"]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in India"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["These services provide support in English, Hindi and additional languages."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also download the ",["112 India mobile app","https://www.india.gov.in/directory/helpline"]," which can track your location to support response in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Further helpline numbers are available on the ",["National Portal of India.","https://www.india.gov.in/directory/helpline"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Indian Ministry of Tourism helpline"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 1800 11 1363"]},{"k":"p","s":["The tourism helpline provides:"]},{"k":"li","s":["advice on reputable sites and services"]},{"k":"li","s":["the option to make a complaint about a company"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=India"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=India"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?country=India&serviceType=translatorsInterpreters"]," in India"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in India","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-pack-india"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in India","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/india-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of rape or sexual assault abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/rape-and-sexual-assault-abroad"]," or ",["victim of rape or sexual assault in India","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/rape-and-sexual-assault-in-india-information-for-victims/india-information-for-survivors-of-rape-and-sexual-assault"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/india/british-high-commission-new-delhi"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in India","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-india"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":38498,"change":"This travel advice has been reviewed for accuracy, with minor amendments made throughout, including updated information on access permits, scams, trekking in India, air and rail travel, India-Pakistan border area and Western India and healthcare in India (‘Entry requirements’,‘Safety and security’ a"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"c6b5b659a5043c6967981fa72723abc6524a54a730b6d6efecdcbc074570df33","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua","bytes":50892,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Nicaragua travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-05T14:10:53+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["UK government support"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no resident British diplomatic mission in Nicaragua, and FCDO cannot give in-person support. If you need emergency help or have passport-related issues, contact the ",["British Embassy in San Jose, Costa Rica","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-in-costa-rica"],", via this ",["contact form","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/home"],". Replacement travel documents may take up to 4 weeks longer than normal to reach you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help British nationals make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Nicaragua’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Nicaragua set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Nicaraguan Embassy in the UK","https://www.facebook.com/embaniclondon/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Nicaragua, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Nicaragua for up to 90 days without a visa. You may be refused entry if you do not have an onward ticket."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel company or nearest Nicaraguan embassy what the policy is for entry at the Nicaraguan border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling between Nicaragua, El Salvador, Guatemala and Honduras"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel between Nicaragua, El Salvador, Guatemala and Honduras for up to 90 days without a visa. Read the travel advice for:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["El Salvador","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/el-salvador/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Guatemala","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guatemala/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Honduras","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/honduras/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The 90-day period starts when you enter any of these countries and does not restart when you cross borders. You’ll have to go through immigration checks at borders. If you’re expelled from one of these countries, you’re also excluded from the other 3."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Nicaragua, you can extend your stay by up to 30 days by paying a fee before the 90 days expires. If you overstay, you may get a fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Nicaragua, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Nicaragua guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/163/nicaragua#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children with Nicaraguan nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children with single or dual Nicaraguan nationality may need certain documents to leave Nicaragua with one parent or a third party. Check with the local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Nicaragua. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. Contact the ",["Nicaraguan Embassy in the UK","https://www.facebook.com/embaniclondon/"]," for more information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electronic cigarettes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a ban on electronic smoking devices such as e-cigarettes in Nicaragua. You cannot import, export, sell, store or use these devices, with or without nicotine. Customs officials can confiscate these products at the border."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Nicaragua"]},{"k":"p","s":["The US dollar, either in cash or travellers cheques, is the only foreign currency freely exchangeable in Nicaragua. Banks do not exchange British pounds."]},{"k":"h","s":["Arrival and departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must pay an arrival tax of 10 US dollars in cash. There is also a departure tax of 35 US dollars, which is normally included in the price of your air ticket."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Nicaragua"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there is no recent history of terrorism in Nicaragua, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations and gatherings can turn violent. It is illegal for foreigners to take part in any sort of political activity in Nicaragua. You can be arrested and detained or deported for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["taking part in a protest"]},{"k":"li","s":["breach of the peace"]},{"k":"li","s":["any activity seen as acting against the government, including political meetings and campaigns"]},{"k":"li","s":["using Nicaragua’s national flag or colours (blue and white) for campaigning or protesting"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations can also lead to travel disruption. Check local information before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals have been affected by violent crime in Nicaragua. Criminals often carry out attacks on people in vehicles. To reduce the risk to yourself and your belongings:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep the windows of your car closed and the doors locked"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid public transport after dark"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when walking around markets, bus stations, around the old cathedral in Managua and in the poorer areas of towns. Do not visit these areas after dark on foot."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are robbed, do not resist, as many criminals carry weapons. If you report the incident to the police, get a signed and stamped copy of the police report."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxi safety and criminal kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of ‘express kidnapping’ if you use an unauthorised taxi. You could be taken hostage and forced to pay cash for your release."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reduce the risk by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["using a radio-dispatched taxi or an authorised taxi with red plates"]},{"k":"li","s":["making sure the driver’s ID number, name and photograph are clearly visible on the dashboard"]},{"k":"li","s":["making a note of the colour and number of the vehicle before you get in"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is a common local practice to share taxis with strangers, but tourists have been robbed when taking taxis called by strangers. Do not take a taxi if it has been called for you by someone you do not know well. You should also avoid using ‘colectivos’ (minibuses)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a woman, use hotels that have staff at the front desk 24 hours a day and have adequate security measures. Read the ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Risks when exchanging money"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk when exchanging money on the street that you could be assaulted or targeted by muggers. There are often money changers with official identification at the front of banks, where there is likely to be better security. You can also withdraw cash in US dollars or Nicaraguan cordobas from ATMs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not become involved with drugs of any kind. Possession of even small quantities can lead to imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flying drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a prohibition on the possession and use of drones. Law 1230 introduced in December 2024 requires people in possession of drones to hand them in to the authorities. You may wish to take legal advice on how to do this."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strong currents off sections of Nicaragua’s Pacific coast and people have drowned. There are no warning signs or lifeguards, and rescue equipment is not readily available."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been fatalities from scuba diving off Nicaragua’s Caribbean coast. If you want to dive, contact a reputable diving company to find out about Nicaraguan waters. Nicaragua’s only hyperbaric chamber is in Puerto Cabezas, a 5-hour speedboat ride from Corn Island."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive a car, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You cannot drive or import right-hand-drive vehicles into Nicaragua."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Nicaragua. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence.","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards and road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of driving is low and the condition of vehicles, particularly taxis and buses, is poor. There’s a risk of drivers failing to give way and driving dangerously, including under the influence of alcohol."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions are generally poor. There is no street lighting on the main highways between major cities and only minimal street lighting in towns. Avoid driving at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re involved in a serious or fatal road traffic accident, you’re likely to be detained while it is investigated."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Boat and ferry travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although local law requires operators of water transport to have insurance, some still do not carry recognised insurance. Check the operator’s insurance cover before beginning your journey."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"]," for information about how to prepare, and how to react if there is a warning."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The hurricane season normally runs from June to November. Monitor the National Hurricane Center forecasts and the ",["World Meteorological Organization warnings","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/cgn/index.html"],". Follow the advice of local authorities and obey evacuation orders."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["A group of volcanoes, several of which are active, stretches the length of the country, in particular San Cristóbal, Masaya, Cerro Negro, and Telica and Concepción on Ometepe Island. Follow media reports and listen to local authorities if you intend to visit the area."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not hike on volcanoes without an experienced guide."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of earthquakes. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake or tsunami."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Nicaragua","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/163/nicaragua#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Nicaragua","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/163/nicaragua"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot use British-issued prescriptions locally. To find a pharmacy (‘farmacia’), search online for the nearest big national chain, such as FarmaValue, Farmacia MEDCO, Farmacia Saba, Farmacia Kielsa, or Farmacia El Ahorro."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Nicaragua"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public hospitals in Nicaragua are not well equipped, except for some hospitals in Managua. Emergency medical treatment is normally free in a public hospital but you will be charged for private health care. You may have difficulties without a good understanding of Spanish."]},{"k":"p","s":["Private hospitals usually take payment for healthcare up front and in cash. A few private hospitals will accept major credit cards. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Nicaragua","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/hospitals-in-nicaragua"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Nicaragua"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Nicaragua"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Nicaragua"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Nicaragua"]," in Nicaragua"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Nicaragua","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nicaragua-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Nicaragua","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/prisoner-pack-nicaragua"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/nicaragua/british-embassy-san-jose"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":13926,"change":"Updated information on visa requirements when travelling between Nicaragua, El Salvador, Guatemala and Honduras ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-sudan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"7d9d0fe4dff631cb88f352e3fa59d4313cedf66c3147659a7795ac7f205c4d2c","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/south-sudan","bytes":55349,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"South Sudan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-26T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-25T10:10:08+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to South Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to South Sudan due to the risk of armed violence and criminality."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more about ",["safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-sudan/safety-and-security"]," in South Sudan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political and security situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political and security situation remains unpredictable. Political tensions are high and the security situation across the country could deteriorate rapidly and unpredictably."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the unstable security situation deteriorates, routes into and out of South Sudan may be blocked. Juba airport may close or be inaccessible. Flights may be cancelled at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regional developments may also affect international transport. For example, in 2019 and 2023, events in Sudan caused South Sudan’s airspace to close temporarily."]},{"k":"p","s":["Consular assistance to British nationals is severely limited in South Sudan. In person consular assistance is not available."]},{"k":"h","s":["If you are in South Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO continues to advise against all travel to South Sudan. If you choose to remain in South Sudan, you do so at your own risk. You should have a personal emergency plan that does not rely on the UK government. This includes the ability to leave the country or to shelter in place, if you judge that to be the safer choice. Make sure to keep all travel documentation up to date, stock up on essential supplies, and monitor the local situation."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not assume that FCDO will be able to provide assistance to leave the country in the event of serious unrest or crisis."]},{"k":"p","s":["If there is civil disorder, stay somewhere safe and limit your movements as much as possible. Avoid all protests, political rallies and large gatherings, and follow the instructions of local authorities and security services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-sudan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel against Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of South Sudan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in South Sudan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["South Sudanese Embassy in the UK","https://embrss.org.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter South Sudan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the day you arrive and have at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter or travel through South Sudan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["apply online for a South Sudan visa","https://evisa.gov.ss/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["apply through the South Sudanese Embassy for a visa","https://embrss.org.uk/immigration-and-passports/visa-information-requirements"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to extend your visa, contact the Ministry of the Interior in person:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ministry of the Interior, Airport Road, Juba Phone: +211 (0)926 388 499 Email: info@mol.gov.ss"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to work in South Sudan, see information on work permits from the Ministry of Labour."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the police"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must register at a local police station if you’re in South Sudan for 5 days or more."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter South Sudan, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination."]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s South Sudan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/202/south-sudan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["In May 2026, neighbouring countries ( ",["Democratic Republic of Congo","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"]," and ",["Uganda","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda"],") reported Ebola cases, including in areas close to the border with South Sudan (Western Equatoria State). If crossing a land border from DRC or Uganda into South Sudan, you may encounter health screening measures such as temperature checks and a request to provide a brief travel history."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Juba International Airport, some airlines are now asking passengers departing the country to complete a health declaration form. Some countries have heightened health screening for travellers coming from South Sudan. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK’s Returning Workers Scheme has been activated, due to the outbreak of Ebola disease. Returning health and humanitarian workers should check the latest at ",["UK’s Returning Workers Scheme","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/ebola-returning-workers-scheme"]," before returning to the UK. Due to the proximity of South Sudan to affected areas, South Sudan is also covered by the scheme."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Health Security Agency has ",["Ebola information for humanitarian or healthcare workers","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ebola-virus-disease-information-for-workers-in-at-risk-countries"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["COVID-19"]},{"k":"p","s":["On rare occasions, some travellers have been asked to show proof of their COVID-19 vaccination. You can get proof of vaccination:"]},{"k":"li","s":["from your GP or Health and Social Care Trust"]},{"k":"li","s":["at the location you were vaccinated"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Scotland, through the ",["COVID-19 vaccination helpline","https://publichealthscotland.scot/our-areas-of-work/health-protection/infectious-diseases/covid-19/covid-19-vaccinations/covid-19-vaccine-information-and-resources/vaccine-resources-in-other-languages-and-alternative-formats/"]," or an ",["online customer service portal","https://vacs.nhs.scot/csp"]]},{"k":"li","s":["in Northern Ireland, from your GP or Health and Social Care Trust"]},{"k":"h","s":["Harassment related to vaccine certificates, visas and work permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["South Sudan’s security services have harassed, detained and expelled foreign nationals, including non-governmental organisation staff and journalists, when they enter or leave Juba airport. These incidents are often linked to proof of yellow fever vaccination, and visa and work permit issues. Make sure you have the correct visa and any required work permit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of South Sudan. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. Contact the ",["South Sudanese Embassy in the UK","https://embrss.org.uk/"]," for information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in South Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in South Sudan, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreigners. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political and security situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political and security situation remains unpredictable. Political tensions are high and the security situation across the country could deteriorate rapidly and unpredictably."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the unstable security situation deteriorates, routes into and out of South Sudan may be blocked. Juba airport may close or be inaccessible. Flights may be cancelled at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regional developments may also affect international transport. For example, in 2019 and 2023, events in Sudan caused South Sudan’s airspace to close temporarily."]},{"k":"h","s":["If you are in South Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO continues to advise against all travel to South Sudan. If you choose to remain in South Sudan, you do so at your own risk. You should have a personal emergency plan that does not rely on the UK government. This includes the ability to leave the country or to shelter in place, if you judge that to be the safer choice. Make sure to keep all travel documentation up to date, stock up on essential supplies, and monitor the local situation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If there is civil disorder, stay somewhere safe and limit your movements as much as possible. Avoid all protests, political rallies and large gatherings, and follow the instructions of local authorities and security services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Robbery and assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of serious crime such as robbery and assault in Juba and other urban areas, particularly at night and on public transport. There are drive-by robberies by individuals or groups on motorbikes."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular attacks by armed groups and accidents on the Juba-Nimule road, the main supply route from Uganda into South Sudan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals in South Sudan are often armed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnapping and violence against aid workers"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is extremely difficult for businesses and non-governmental organisations to work in South Sudan. Although the number of aid workers killed in targeted attacks has fallen in recent years, South Sudan remains one of the most dangerous environments in the world for aid workers. There are incidents of criminal kidnapping, violence, intimidation and arbitrary detention."]},{"k":"h","s":["Road checkpoints"]},{"k":"p","s":["Checkpoints operated by soldiers or other armed men are common in and around Juba, particularly after dark. Armed men at checkpoints have been known to demand money from drivers and abuse people, especially women. Roadblocks can create volatile and dangerous situations and are often put up after sunset, so it advisable not to travel after dark."]},{"k":"h","s":["Armed conflict"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed conflict, including violence targeting civilians is common throughout South Sudan. Fighting often starts quickly and unpredictably. Follow instructions from local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 4 March 2025, there were reports of intense fighting in Nasir, Upper Nile State."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the 16 and 17 January 2025, there was sporadic gunfire and looting across major towns, including in areas of Juba city."]},{"k":"p","s":["To keep yourself informed of the latest developments, follow and contact FCDO travel on ",["X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"],", ",["Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"],", and ",["Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"],". You can also ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-sudan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines and unexploded weapons"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk from landmines or unexploded cluster bombs in some areas of South Sudan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Affected states include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Central Equatoria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Eastern Equatoria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Jonglei"]},{"k":"li","s":["Central and Eastern Equatoria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lakes"]},{"k":"li","s":["Upper Nile"]},{"k":"li","s":["Warrap"]},{"k":"li","s":["Western Equatoria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most areas with unexploded weapons have been marked and signposted, but there may still be small, previously unidentified hazardous areas in remote places."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious near areas with unexploded weapons or where there was previously heavy fighting. Do not enter marked areas with landmines or other explosives. Do not touch any suspicious objects (even to move them to a safer place)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Limited UK government support"]},{"k":"p","s":["Consular support is severely limited in South Sudan. The British Embassy in Juba does not have a consular section. If you are in South Sudan and need urgent help from the UK government, contact the ",["British High Commission in Nairobi, Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-high-commission-nairobi"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you decide to travel to South Sudan, make sure you carefully consider the threats and have reasonable, proportionate mitigation measures in place. Most international organisations in South Sudan employ a security manager to help keep employees safe."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police can ask to see photo ID. Always carry a colour copy of your passport with you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for using or trafficking drugs in South Sudan, including the death penalty and life imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take photographs close to government buildings, military installations, bridges, airports, public utilities (including petrol stations) and other sensitive areas. Plainclothes public security officers operate in Juba and across South Sudan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are not culturally accepted. Same-sex sexual activity between men is illegal and punishable by a prison sentence of up to 14 years. LGBT+ travellers are at risk of discrimination and violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["International credit and debit cards are not widely accepted, although some of the newer hotels and supermarkets are starting to."]},{"k":"p","s":["ATMs are hard to find, and it is often not possible to use international cards. You can use your credit or debit card to withdraw money in some supermarkets. Bring large denomination US dollars (clean, unblemished notes dated 2017 onwards). Dollars are acceptable currency in many places, but shops and restaurants are likely to refuse notes that are marked in any way."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is extremely dangerous to drive in South Sudan due to armed robbery, violent attacks and poor driving standards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are well below those in the UK and other European countries. Very few roads are surfaced and maintained, particularly outside Juba. Residential areas usually have dirt roads. Road traffic accidents are common, particularly on the Juba-Nimule road."]},{"k":"p","s":["At night there is almost no street lighting, and many vehicles have no lights. Motor vehicles share the road with pedestrians, donkey carts and rickshaw-style cabs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although drivers should have a licence and insurance, many do not. Make sure you have adequate insurance. Your insurance could be invalidated if you travel against FCDO advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in South Sudan. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public transport, including small buses, vans and motorbike taxis (‘boda-bodas’), is extremely unsafe. Drivers are reckless, traffic accidents are common and vehicles are in poor condition. There is also a high risk of mugging. Avoid public transport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the rainy season from April to November, most roads outside of Juba become impassable. There is a risk of being cut off by floods in areas outside the capital, particularly in Unity, Warrap, Jonglei and Upper Nile states. There is also a risk of flash flooding."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["South Sudan does not have an emergency medical public phone number. There are limited private ambulance services, but you will have to register with a private clinic first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccination recommendations for South Sudan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/202/south-sudan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in South Sudan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/202/south-sudan"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["cholera"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of malaria in South Sudan is high. You can find more information about malaria on ",["TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/202/south-sudan#Malaria"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The South Sudanese Ministry of Health has issued a ",["statement","https://moh.gov.ss/news-details_copypress.php?id=18"]," about the outbreak of cholera. You can find more information on cholera on ",["TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/202/south-sudan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in Eastern Equatoria near the border with Uganda, where there are mountains of over 3,000 metres. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in South Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Health facilities are extremely limited throughout South Sudan. Many medical issues require medical evacuation to neighbouring hubs (Nairobi, Kenya, and Kampala, Uganda, are the most common). During the rainy season, flights are often forced to remain on the ground for hours. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any treatment abroad, medical evacuation and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in South Sudan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/south-sudan-doctors"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in South Sudan"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no central emergency numbers in South Sudan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from FCDO."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["English-speaking lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=South%20Sudan"]," in South Sudan"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in South Sudan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/south-sudan-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in South Sudan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/south-sudan-in-prison-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being a ",["victim of rape or sexual assault in South Sudan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/south-sudan-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault/south-sudan-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/south-sudan/british-embassy-of-juba"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-sudan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":18265,"change":"Updated information about Ebola ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/what-the-us-midterms-result-means-for-the-ukraine-war-295705":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"95693a33a6f83737a80f2c914fb5c444aed4bc8ec8ab0e0618f94f3f45e7ebad","read":"https://theconversation.com/what-the-us-midterms-result-means-for-the-ukraine-war-295705","bytes":179821,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What the US midterms result means for the Ukraine war","by":[{"n":"Michael Cox","r":"Founding Director of LSE IDEAS and Emeritus Professor of International Relations, London School of Economics and Political Science"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T14:43:34Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The US midterm elections have shifted the balance of power in Congress, delivering a massive blow to Donald Trump and his Republican party. This has implications both at home and possibly abroad, including for US policy towards Ukraine; an issue that was hardly mentioned during the campaigns."]},{"k":"p","s":["But even if ",["Ukraine","https://theconversation.com/topics/ukraine-8201"]," did not figure much in the election, the question in US politics of what to do about the war has not gone away. Indeed, in the weeks and months before the result was announced, Trump had been busily rowing back on US support for Ukraine. This was despite much opposition, even from some Republicans."]},{"k":"p","s":["Crucial intelligence to Kyiv about Russian strikes ",["was cut off","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm2d6e62p49do"],", before later being reinstated, while ",["critical military aid","https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2026/10/20/white-house-blocks-transfer-of-patriot-missiles-to-ukraine/"]," was reduced. Trump also ",["decided to suspend","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9p8gz7zx4peo"]," several sanctions on Russia."]},{"k":"p","s":["This move was ",["denounced","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/trump-suspends-new-russia-sanctions-deal-purchase-diesel-citing-nation-rcna603991"]," by President Volodymyr Zelensky of Ukraine as only helping Russia, but justified by Trump as being “in the national interests of the United States” and also a decision that might help his party’s electoral chances by reducing gas prices."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the end, none of this helped Trump and the Republicans. Yet few commentators believe that the midterm results, disastrous though they have been for Trump, will have very much impact on his foreign policy outlook and his policy towards Ukraine in particular."]},{"k":"p","s":["“The Trump administration’s foreign policy is like a car going down the highway,” ",["said","https://www.theparliamentmagazine.eu/news/article/the-democrats-won-americas-midterms-that-wont-alter-trumps-position-on-ukraine-or-europe"]," James Green, a research fellow at the Centre for European Reform and former Congressional aide in Washington, recently. “Congress has the ability to slow that car down, maybe make it put on a turn signal, but it’s going to be very difficult for Congress to change the overall route over the next two years.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["In part, this has to do with how foreign policy is determined in the US. Congress is not without some influence. It can hold hearings, subpoena executive branch officials, as well as exercise control over the purse. Yet as commander-in-chief and head of state with a vast foreign policy bureaucracy supporting him, the president retains significant ",["foreign policy powers","https://theconversation.com/donald-trumps-republicans-suffer-landslide-defeat-what-this-means-for-the-world-295769"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Democrats are also unlikely to make Ukraine front and centre after the midterms. They will have other more important fish to fry, the most critical being how to make sure they come up with a candidate and programme that will win them the White House in 2028."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet Ukraine is a cause which many Democrats and quite a few Republicans have championed for some time. Nor are they likely to forget what ordinary Americans think about Russia and its leader, Vladimir Putin."]},{"k":"p","s":["The war in Ukraine may not be something they think about on a daily basis. On the other hand, as the ",["Pew Research Center","https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2025/04/17/how-americans-view-russia-and-putin/"]," showed in 2025, 67% of Americans distrust Putin while six in ten view Russia as an enemy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Democrats may not wish to become embroiled in a European war. But having just scored a sweeping landslide victory, they may well calculate there is a good deal of political mileage to be had now in escalating their attack on a weakened Trump if his foreign policy towards Russia and Ukraine continues in their view to reward an aggressor while making the victim of that aggression look like an obstacle to a settlement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pushing for a peace deal?"]},{"k":"p","s":["If the midterms result presents a series of opportunities for the Democrats, while posing a challenge to Trump, it also presents Putin with a possible opportunity. The Russian leader may well try and exploit Trump’s domestic position by offering some kind of settlement that would allow the US president to claim a victory."]},{"k":"p","s":["US, Chinese and Russian officials ",["have already been","https://www.independent.co.uk/voices/putin-trump-china-xi-russia-moscow-washington-banquet-b3056361.html"]," holding talks about a summit when the heads of state travel to China for the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (Apec) summit later in November. Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov ",["has said Russia","https://www.reutersconnect.com/collection/kremlin-hopes-plans-for-us-russia-china-leaders-meeting-will-be-finalised-soon/dGFnOnJldXRlcnMuY29tLDIwMjY6bmV3c21sX1ZBNTI4MDAzMTEyMDI2UlAx"]," hopes to finalise the meeting in the coming days."]},{"k":"p","s":["Trump is similarly keen on such a meeting. He told reporters in October that Ukraine would be discussed at the meeting, ",["adding","https://www.politico.eu/article/moscow-is-helping-arrange-us-russia-china-meeting-spokesperson-peskov-says/"],": “I would meet in order – anything I can do to end the war, whether somebody is there or not, whatever I can do to end the war.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["This might sound reasonable enough. However, deciding the fate of a sovereign country which won’t be at the negotiating table, and coming to some kind of ",["“great power” deal","https://theconversation.com/why-trump-xi-and-putin-cant-carve-up-the-world-like-the-big-three-leaders-of-1945-295632"]," with two authoritarian countries that involves Ukraine losing 20% of its territory, is almost certainly something an emboldened Democratic party in Congress will not take lying down."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nor, according to most military experts, would it be wise to concede anything to Russia when its war against Ukraine appears to have run into the ground. According to the Institute for the Study of War, ",["Russia may have","https://understandingwar.org/research/russia-ukraine/the-myth-of-inevitable-russian-victory/"]," “secured a temporary advantage in the skies over Ukraine through their jet-powered drones and the shortage of Patriot missiles that can intercept their ballistic missiles”."]},{"k":"p","s":["But as the institute also points out, unless western military aid dries up entirely, a Russian victory is by no means inevitable. A war that most experts, including the CIA, predicted would be over in a matter of months is thus likely to go on."]},{"k":"p","s":["Trump is unlikely to change his mind about Russia and Ukraine. Russia in his mind’s eye will continue to be regarded as a potential partner, and Ukraine a country that has taken assistance from the US and ",["given","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-trump-says-u-s-has-gotten-nothing-from-ukraine-other-than-high-diesel-urging-deal"]," “absolutely nothing back except grief”."]},{"k":"p","s":["But now, with his back to the wall politically and the Democrats in charge of Congress in a country that has just passed a decisive verdict on his presidency, shaping his own agenda in relation to Russia and Ukraine is likely to prove more difficult."]}],"chars":5579},"https://theconversation.com/in-antarcticas-ice-free-areas-even-footprints-can-damage-rare-microscopic-ecosystems-296045":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T20:22Z","sha":"85f8653da9a2c884f045532f29e0d19557ba5f196b3dfa0a3f0981c06b1ab416","read":"https://theconversation.com/in-antarcticas-ice-free-areas-even-footprints-can-damage-rare-microscopic-ecosystems-296045","bytes":176239,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"In Antarctica’s ice-free areas, even footprints can damage rare microscopic ecosystems","by":[{"n":"Angela McGaughran","r":"Senior Lecturer in Population Genomics, University of Waikato"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T19:10:18Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The usual advice for people visiting wilderness areas is to leave nothing but footprints."]},{"k":"p","s":["But as our new ",["study","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0944501326003575#bib31"]," shows, even footprints may disturb rare ecosystems in Antarctica and cause irreversible changes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Antarctica harbours some of the world’s rarest and most precious ecosystems, including the ",["permafrost soils of the vast, ice-free McMurdo Dry Valleys","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0016706107002960"]," – one of the driest deserts on Earth."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite the harsh conditions, the ice-cemented soil layers are home to unique, localised microbial communities and tiny spineless creatures such as nematodes, tardigrades and rotifers that survive in thin water films around grains of sand."]},{"k":"p","s":["Environmental protection is a key focus of ",["Antarctic governance","https://www.ats.aq/e/protocol.html"]," and quarantine and decontamination protocols prescribe comprehensive inspection and cleaning of footwear and other field gear prior to departure to the continent."]},{"k":"p","s":["But such protocols are in place to primarily prevent people from bringing and spreading new invasive species in Antarctica. Our study focused on the possibility of people redistributing local microbial communities between sites and unwittingly disturbing fragile ecosystems."]},{"k":"h","s":["Disrupting locally adapted ecosystems"]},{"k":"p","s":["While the number of established non-native species in Antarctica is low compared with most continents, ",["biological invasions are on the rise","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/ddi.12593"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At ",["least a dozen","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10531-015-0896-6"]," non-native land invertebrates, including soil-dwelling springtails and mites, and ",["several plant species","https://environments.aq/publications/terrestrial-non-native-species-in-antarctica-introduction-impact-and-management-response/"]," have been recorded south of 60°S, particularly near research stations and heavily visited areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Human activity – including scientific operations, logistics and tourism – is the primary route of invasion for non-native species. Once introduced, climate warming is expected to increase the chances these species will survive Antarctic conditions and spread."]},{"k":"p","s":["But for now, perhaps the biggest threat is intra-continental transfer. This is when endemic Antarctic species that are already locally adapted spread beyond their usual distribution ranges."]},{"k":"p","s":["The most likely candidates for this kind of spread are microbes, which play a fundamental role in ecosystems as primary producers and nutrient cyclers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The extreme conditions of Antarctic soils mean that even common and globally distributed bacterial lineages have to adapt to the point that they evolve into strains ",["found nowhere else","https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2611373123#sec-3"]," on Earth. Within the Dry Valleys, communities are so specific that each valley has a ",["unique microbial signature","https://www.nature.com/articles/ismej2011170"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Microbial DNA tracks movement between valleys"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study asked whether people transfer microbes between valleys and potentially disrupt local assemblages. We compared microbial species identified in local soil with those found on surfaces of field equipment, helicopter skids and boots."]},{"k":"p","s":["In one analysis, we found that 73% of swabbed footwear harboured DNA from microbes we also detected at upstream locations in a single day of operational movements."]},{"k":"p","s":["While cleaning and disinfection changed the microbial communities present on field equipment, we found this did not completely eliminate the transfer of microbial taxa between gear and local soils."]},{"k":"p","s":["Field operations in the Dry Valleys are therefore likely contributing to the movement of locally adapted and valley-specific microbial communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["We haven’t yet determined the potential ecological impact of our findings. But these results clearly emphasise the importance of biosecurity monitoring and decontamination protocols across Antarctic field programmes."]},{"k":"p","s":["New Zealanders have accepted the need to disinfect boots to prevent the spread of pathogens such as kauri dieback disease."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Antarctica’s Dry Valleys, we need to strengthen contamination protocols to disinfect boots and field gear if more than one site is visited, while also upping biosecurity monitoring for microbes and other easily dispersed species."]}],"chars":3782}};
